pokeheartgold-wideprotos.patch (GENERATED by tools/pokehg_protos.py --write on a fresh tree with every other patch
applied; tools/pokehg_gen.py applies it last): pret's HGSS C declares many functions in other files or headers with a
32-bit int where the definition takes or returns a pointer, or the reverse (2,311 slots of 1,816 functions on
1c6447d57; e4bbe3c9e: 2,317 of 1,819; 90222550d: 2,320 of 1,822; cc952ee13: 2,309 of 1,794; bc7fa4386: 4,002 of 3,191; 95d5f7f1d: 4,264 of 3,383). On the DS both are 4 bytes; on a 64-bit host the int side truncates the pointer: the caller passes 32 bits
through an int prototype, or the callee reads its pointer argument as s32 (the first: sub_02031B3C(s32) called through
a pointer prototype, its s32 then given to sub_020325CC(void *) declared (s32): SIGSEGV at frame 0). Each 32-bit int
of such a slot, the definition's and every declaration's, becomes uintptr_t, so the value passes whole both ways; --chains build/port/linux-hgss then widens the
32-bit locals such a value is stored in (261; e4bbe3c9e: 255; 90222550d: 256; cc952ee13: 223), and the extern data pass the int declarations of pointer globals (4).
The list for the HGSS side (the real fix is the right type): `python3 tools/pokehg_protos.py --report OUT.tsv`.
Remake it after a re-pin or a change to the patches before it.
